.TH LIBUTF8_REPLACE_INVALID 3 LIBUTF8
.SH NAME
LIBUTF8_REPLACE_INVALID - Replace decoded invalid Unicode codepoints

.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <libutf8.h>

#define \fBLIBUTF8_REPLACE_INVALID\fP /* implementation omitted */
.fi

.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B LIBUTF8_REPLACE_INVALID
macro is a flag for
.BR libutf8_decode (3)
and
.BR libutf8_decode_mem (3).
It causes those functions to replace a decoded invalid Unicode codepoint with
.BR LIBUTF8_REPLACEMENT_CHARACTER_CODEPOINT (3)
rather than reject it.
.PP
The flag applies to non-character codepoints (see
.BR libutf8_is_noncharacter (3)
for definition) and UTF-16 surrogates.
It does not make illegal byte sequences, overlong encodings,
or codepoints above
.B LIBUTF8_ULTIMATE_CODEPOINT
valid.

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR libutf8 (7),
.BR LIBUTF8_RETURN_INVALID (3),
.BR LIBUTF8_REPLACEMENT_CHARACTER_CODEPOINT (3),
.BR libutf8_is_continuation (3),
.BR libutf8_decode (3),
.BR libutf8_decode_mem (3)
